      "name": "EmotionalDistressSignal",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.6,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A distinct emotional-tone axis that could add value. However groundedness is weaker: IMDB-0001 and IMDB-0004 are debatable, and IMDB-0005 ('distress_evident') reflects plot heartache, not reviewer distress, an over-reading of the source."
    },
    {
      "name": "WasteRegretLanguage",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Waste/regret language is a meaningful negative-satisfaction signal. But IMDB-0002 and IMDB-0003 marked 'waste_or_regret_expressed' without clear waste/regret wording in the shown text, suggesting inferred rather than grounded values."
    },
    {
      "name": "CriticalTargetBreadth",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Whether criticism is broad/systematic vs narrow is a solid analytical axis correlating with dissatisfaction depth. Sample values are reasonable readings of the reviews."
    },
    {
      "name": "SystemicFailureAttribution",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Distinguishing isolated vs fundamental failure is useful for modeling. Somewhat conceptually overlapping with CriticalTargetBreadth but not a mere restatement. Sample values are defensible readings."
    },
    {
      "name": "direct_condemnation_signal",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.1,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "This is essentially a duplicate of DirectCondemnation with identical value vocabulary and matching per-row values in all samples. Redundant restatement adds no analytical leverage, so usefulness is very low despite being grounded."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.65,
  "source_groundedness": 0.72,
  "rationale": "Most columns provide genuine distinct axes (condemnation harshness, criticism breadth, failure attribution, waste/regret) that plausibly relate to negative IMDb satisfaction and offer real grouping/modeling leverage. The clear weakness is 'direct_condemnation_signal', a near-exact duplicate of 'DirectCondemnation'. Groundedness is generally sound as categorisations of the review text, but EmotionalDistressSignal and WasteRegretLanguage show some over-reading/inferred values (e.g. plot-level heartache read as reviewer distress; waste/regret asserted without supporting wording), pulling the table-level groundedness down modestly."
